  "graded_by": [
    {
      "unit": "U3",
      "test": "worker/tests/test_spool.py — every end the worker originates or observes from outside TSB is spooled atomically and fsync'd before it is acted on, in exactly this shape"
    },
    {
      "unit": "U2",
      "test": "core/internal/session/spool_test.go — the core reads the spool before any E10 decision, writes the end marker and session.disconnect stamped ended_at, and deletes the entry"
    }
  ],
  "description": "The spool (session model §11 orphan_timeout, §15): an end while the core is away is written to disk, because after orphan_timeout ends a connection's last session the connection lingers out and the worker exits — a spool in memory would die with it and the returning core would read E10 worker_lost. Exactly the pairs a worker can name: killed / orphan, idle or unattended (the timers it runs while the core is gone) and terminated / target_closed or connection_lost. The core persists every end it asks for itself, so owner, admin and worker_lost never appear. last_seq, out_bytes and last_out_ts let the core declare a gap before the end marker when output was lost; a session with no output has all three 0.",
  "corpus": [
    "session model §11",
    "session model §12",
    "session model §15",
    "lang-arch §6.4",
    "immortality §4.3"
  ],
